\caption(Actual original-event states, including the unsent200-byte tail.)
\alttext(Blue points count buffered bytes; red points count sent unacknowledged bytes, ending at200 and300 respectively.)

> Compare equal completed payloads with explicit final ACKs

Append ACK300 to release the original200-byte buffer, then ACK200 to acknowledge
that final packet. Both Nagle and the immediate-write baseline now send and
acknowledge all600 bytes. Nagle emits three packets100,300,200; the baseline
emits six100-byte packets. Under the explicitly assumed40 header bytes per
packet, the counts are120 and240 header bytes. TCP/IP options and other real
protocol details are outside this fixed-header arithmetic.

This illustrates the tradeoff between delaying small writes and reducing packet
overhead. Without event times and a real receiver model, it cannot quantify the
delay or predict a throughput gain.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/nagle_drained.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto events = dm::algorithms::nagle_demo_events(true);
    auto with = dm::algorithms::nagle_analyze(events, 500);
    auto without = dm::algorithms::nagle_analyze(events, 500, false);
    std::print("| sender | actual packets | written | sent | unsent | outstanding | assumed header bytes " "|\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Nagle | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} " "|\n| immediate | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               with.packets, with.written, with.sent, with.buffered,
               with.unacked, dm::algorithms::nagle_header_bytes(with),
               without.packets, without.written, without.sent, without.buffered,
               without.unacked, dm::algorithms::nagle_header_bytes(without));
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({double(dm::algorithms::nagle_header_bytes(
                                             with)),
                                      double(dm::algorithms::nagle_header_bytes(
                                             without))}, {"Nagle", "immediate"},
                                     "assumed header bytes");
    p.title("Explicitly drained600-byte payload: fixed-header comparison").x_label("sender model").y_label("40 assumed bytes per actual packet").save_svg("build/nagle_drained.svg");
}
```
